<title>GERMANY: Audi sees 1996 profit up 25 pct at least.</title>
<headline>Audi sees 1996 profit up 25 pct at least.</headline>
<dateline>INGOLSTADT, Germany 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Audi AG, a subsidiary of Volkswagen AG, said on Friday its group pre-tax profit for 1996 would be at least 25 percent above the 1995 level.</p>
<p>The carmaker posted a pre-tax profit of 589 million marks ($377.9 million) and a net profit of 111 million marks for 1995.  </p>
<p>Separately, Audi's employee newspaper &quot;audi mobil&quot; said the carmaker's prospects for 1997 were good. Unit sales in Germany had increased in 1996 and sales abroad had grown at an even faster rate, the magazine said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
